#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:18 ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:99
#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:143
msgid "Is it rated?"
msgstr "レーティングは反映されますか？"

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:20 ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:154
msgid "How are scores calculated?"
msgstr "成績はどのように算出されるのですか？"

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:22
msgid ""
"A win has a base score of 2 points, a draw 1 point, and a loss is worth no "
"points."
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:24
msgid ""
"If you win two games consecutively you will start a double point streak, "
"represented by a flame icon."
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:26
msgid ""
"The following games will continue to be worth double points until you fail "
"to win a game."
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:28
msgid ""
"That is, a win will be worth 4 points, a draw 2 points, and a loss will "
"still not award any points."
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:30
msgid ""
"For example, two wins followed by a draw will be worth 6 points: 2 + 2 + (2 "
"× 1)"
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:33
msgid ""
"(Janggi scores are different. A win has a base score of 7 points, and a loss"
" is worth no points. Point counting win and loss worth 4 and 2 points "
"respectively.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:37
msgid "Arena Berserk"
msgstr "アリーナバーサク"

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:40
msgid ""
"When a player clicks the Berserk button at the beginning of the game, they "
"lose half of their clock time, but the win is worth one extra tournament "
"point."
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:47
msgid ""
"Going Berserk in time controls with an increment also cancels the increment."
" (1+2 is an exception, it gives 1+0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:52
msgid "Berserk is not available for games with zero initial time (0+1, 0+2)."
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:54
msgid ""
"Berserk only grants an extra point if you play at least 7 moves in the game."
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:55 ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:117
msgid "How is the winner decided?"
msgstr "勝者はどのようにして決まるのですか？"

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:58
msgid ""
"The player(s) with the most points after the tournament's set time limit "
"will be announced the winner(s)."
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:65
msgid ""
"When two or more players have the same number of points, the tournament "
"performance is the tie break."
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:67
msgid "How does the pairing work?"
msgstr "マッチングの仕組みはどうなっていますか？"

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:68
msgid ""
"At the beginning of the tournament, players are paired based on their "
"rating."
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:72
msgid ""
"As soon as you finish a game, return to the tournament lobby: you will then "
"be paired with a player close to your ranking. This ensures minimum wait "
"time, however you may not face all other players in the tournament."
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:77
msgid ""
"Play fast and return to the lobby to play more games and win more points."
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:78 ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:124
#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:211
msgid "How does it end?"
msgstr "終了条件は何ですか？"

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:81
msgid ""
"The tournament has a countdown clock. When it reaches zero, the tournament "
"rankings are frozen, and the winner is announced. Games in progress must be "
"finished, however they don't count for the tournament."
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:85
msgid "Other important rules"
msgstr "他の重要なルール"

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:88
msgid ""
"There is a countdown for your first move. Failing to make a move within this"
" time will forfeit the game to your opponent."
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:93
msgid ""
"Drawing the game before each player has moved 5 times will earn neither "
"player any points."
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:101
msgid "How does round-robin work?"
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:102
msgid ""
"In a round-robin tournament, each player can play one game against every "
"other player."
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:103
msgid "How do I play a game?"
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:106
msgid ""
"To play, click the cell in the table where you and the opponent you want to "
"play against meet. You can schedule a date and time of the game or start the"
" game right away by sending a challenge to your opponent."
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:110
msgid "How are points given?"
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:113
msgid ""
"You get 2 points for a win, 1 for a draw, and 0 for a loss. Every match "
"counts toward your total score."
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:120
msgid ""
"The player with the most points at the end wins. If players have the same "
"number of points, the one with the higher tournament performance is ranked "
"higher."
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:127
msgid ""
"The tournament ends when all scheduled games are completed, or when the "
"configured end time is reached. Aborted games do not count and can be "
"scheduled and played again later."
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:136
msgid "Swiss Rules"
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:139
msgid ""
"Swiss tournaments are played in fixed rounds. After each round finishes, the"
" next round starts and players are paired with others on similar score."
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:145
msgid "How does pairing work?"
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:146
msgid ""
"Players are paired by Swiss rules with score-group logic and color "
"constraints."
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:150
msgid ""
"You cannot play the same opponent twice, and the system may assign a bye if "
"no legal opponent exists in a round."
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:155
msgid "Most variants use 2/1/0 scoring for win/draw/loss."
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:157
msgid ""
"Janggi uses 7/0 for full win/loss, and 4/2 for point-counting win/loss."
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:161
msgid ""
"A pairing-allocated bye gives full win points. A late join gives a single "
"half-bye compensation even if several rounds were missed."
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:168
msgid ""
"Janggi exception: the late-join half-bye is worth 2 points, pairing-"
"allocated byes give 7 points, and absent rounds give 0 points."
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:172
msgid "Late join and absences"
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:173
msgid ""
"You can join a Swiss after it starts, but only until half of the rounds have"
" been played."
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:177
msgid ""
"Most variants: late joiners get one half-point compensation, and no points "
"for other missed rounds."
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:180
msgid ""
"If you miss a round, you are not paired for that round and score 0 points "
"for it."
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:184
msgid ""
"If you miss an actual Swiss game without moving, you are temporarily blocked"
" from entering a new Swiss until the no-show timeout expires."
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:191
msgid ""
"Absent and late-join placeholder rounds are shown in the standings, and you "
"can still return for later rounds."
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:195
msgid "Tie-break"
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:196
msgid ""
"If players have the same score, Sonneborn-Berger values decide final "
"ranking."
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:200
msgid ""
"Wins count the full score of the opponent, draws count half, and pairing-"
"allocated byes use a virtual-opponent style value. Late-join and absent "
"placeholder rounds do not add tie-break credit."
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:204
msgid "What if the event has too many rounds?"
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:207
msgid ""
"If no legal new pairing can be produced, the Swiss finishes early and the "
"current standings become final."
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentFaq.ts:214
msgid ""
"The tournament ends after all scheduled rounds are completed, or earlier if "
"no further legal pairings exist."
msgstr ""

#: ../client/tournamentForm.ts:8
msgid "Only public user-defined variants can be used in tournaments."
msgstr ""

